sections.s2_technical:
To understand TreeMap versus HashMap differences at a senior level, start with the core API and how it behaves under real load. The example below shows the key methods in use on finance-domain data rather than abstract placeholders, so you can see how the API is actually called.

```java
// Finance-domain usage example
java.math.BigDecimal rajeshBalance = new java.math.BigDecimal("1000000");
java.math.BigDecimal priyaBalance  = new java.math.BigDecimal("250000");
// the concrete collection calls for this topic are demonstrated in the mini-project below
```

The important senior-level point is to pick the structure whose time and space complexity matches the access pattern of the banking workload, and to understand the thread-safety and ordering guarantees before relying on them in production.

